{"id":"sw-438537","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-515e642f-0724-4633-9896-84c961fbdcd0","text":"## Phase 1 complete: audit delivered\n\n`book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md` (in the issue worktree) enumerates every Tier-1 fork in ch01-04 with per-engine notes, `[verify]` flags, and Phase-2 estimates. Method: ch03/ch04 read in full by the lead pass; ch01/ch02 swept by two subagents against the rubric with lead-pass final classification. No chapter files modified (Phase-1 constraint honored).\n\n**Headline numbers:** 11 in-place retrofit items across the four written chapters plus a ch06 rider — **only one is moderate/ceiling-scale** (CH03-F1: the threading model, dedicated-threads+split-pools vs. fibers vs. task graphs, including a learn-bullet promise the body never delivers). The other ten are small (missing Unity lines, an unnamed \"some engines extrapolate\" claim, an implicit device-loss pick). Total ~1,000-1,400 added words — three focused Phase-2 sessions riding each chapter's next revision, far below the feared full restructure.\n\nAlso produced: must-treat obligations for unwritten chapters (ch08: ECS + hybrid-data-model forks with sw-cf6350 benchmark evidence; ch12/15: voxel+mesh rendering thesis), two **outline decisions needing the author** (owning chapter for plugin architecture; owning chapter for code-first game description), and two internal-consistency nits (ch01 RQ7 orphaned concept; ch03 learn-bullet).\n\nAwaiting tophat on the audit before walkthrough/merge; Phase 2 scheduling is the author's call."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:41:22.151212Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2f2873","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ch03 comparison retrofit: threading-model fork + extraction Unity gap (CH03-F1, CH03-F3)","description":"Phase-2 retrofit per `book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md`. **The one moderate item of the audit** — ride along ch03's next revision pass.\n\n- **CH03-F1 (moderate, ~300-400 words):** \"Thread Ownership and the Work-Stealing Pools\" presents the threading strategies as history, not adoptable alternatives. Add the comparison — Naughty Dog fibers (already cited), UE named threads + TaskGraph, Unity main-thread + Job System/Graphics Jobs, Frostbite/id task graphs — and the per-alternative winner rationale for dedicated-threads+split-pools+CSP. **Must also deliver the learn-bullet's unfulfilled promise:** \"why a unified task-graph scheduler is the planned evolution rather than the starting architecture\" (no body text argues this today). Vendor-doc-verify all engine claims. Trim candidate: duplication between the history paragraph and the execution-context walkthrough.\n- **CH03-F3 (small, ~80-120 words):** \"The Extraction Contract\" compares UE `FSceneProxy` and Godot `RenderingServer` but omits Unity (SRP/RenderGraph model) [verify]. Add the Unity line; the full mechanism fork stays owned by ch12 as the prose already promises.\n\nPolicy: tiered comparison rule in `.claude/skills/book/SKILL.md`; ch05 Tick-Stamped Edges is the ceiling; word target is a soft signal.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-2f2873","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["book","revision","chapter-03"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:49:42.130566Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-098dc0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ch04 comparison retrofit: pipeline, extrapolation, device-loss pick, UE tick honesty (CH04-F1/F2/F3/F5, opt. F4)","description":"Phase-2 retrofit per `book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md`. All small; ride along ch04's next revision pass.\n\n- **CH04-F1 (~60-100 w):** \"The Pipeline Concept\" compares UE5 three-stage and ND fibers but omits Unity (main thread + Graphics Jobs / render-thread modes) [verify]. Add the Unity line.\n- **CH04-F2 (~50-100 w):** the \"Extrapolation vs. Interpolation\" callout says \"Some engines extrapolate\" without naming one — currently unfalsifiable. Name and vendor-doc-verify the actual engines/modes (e.g., Source's networked-entity handling, physics prediction modes).\n- **CH04-F3 (~50-80 w):** \"Device Loss\" presents fatal-with-grace vs. recovery walk well but never states Smallworld's own pick. State the v1 pick explicitly (check `docs/architecture/capability-tiers.md`) and the trigger for graduating to the recovery walk.\n- **CH04-F5 (~50-80 w):** the fixed-timestep survey presents the pattern as universal; Unreal's default gameplay tick is variable-delta with optional physics substepping [verify]. One honest sentence in the \"Three Clocks\" survey.\n- **CH04-F4 (optional, ~80-120 w):** render-to-game feedback channel precedent note (Unity `FrameTimingManager`, UE stat/CSV telemetry) [verify] — audit classifies it Tier-2/invention; take only if it earns its words.\n\nPolicy: tiered comparison rule in `.claude/skills/book/SKILL.md`; word target is a soft signal.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a1","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-098dc0","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["book","revision","chapter-04"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:49:49.974187Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e1cbe3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ch01+Ch02 comparison retrofit: wgpu survey, boundary enforcement, boot (CH01-F1, CH02-F1, CH02-F2)","description":"Phase-2 retrofit per `book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md`. All small; one combined session riding either chapter's next revision pass.\n\n- **CH01-F1 (~100-150 w):** \"The Universal Graphics Abstraction\" argues wgpu-vs-in-house-RHI against Unreal's RHI only. Add Unity's platform graphics abstraction and Godot's `RenderingDevice` [verify both] so the \"every engine needs this layer\" claim rests on the full survey.\n- **CH02-F1 (~100-150 w):** \"Layers Become Enforceable Boundaries\" compares UE module graph and Godot server encapsulation but omits Unity (assembly definitions) [verify] and offers no rationale for why compile-time crate boundaries win. Add the Unity line and a per-alternative rationale sentence.\n- **CH02-F2 (~40-60 w):** \"Boot Once\" comparison omits Unity (largely implicit/opaque subsystem init) [verify]. One line.\n\nOptional riders from the audit's ch01/ch02 borderline notes: a one-sentence connective from ch01's engine-divergence catalog (line ~205) to the `FramePacket` pick; ch02 preview pointers to the decided plugin-chapter and ch09 code-first homes.\n\nPolicy: tiered comparison rule in `.claude/skills/book/SKILL.md`.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a2","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-e1cbe3","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["book","revision","chapter-01","chapter-02"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:50:01.444044Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-c65b57","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ch06 rider: handle-lifetime GC comparison (CH03-F2) + budget precedent check","description":"Phase-2 rider per `book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md`; execute with ch06's next revision pass.\n\n- **CH03-F2 (~150-250 w, lands in ch06):** the generational-handle design is argued against refcounting only; the divergent engine lifetime strategies are absent. Add the comparison — UE mark-and-sweep UObject GC + `TWeakObjectPtr`, Unity managed C# GC + native instanceIDs, Godot RIDs + `RefCounted` [verify all] — and argue generational-index handles as the winner per-alternative (no GC pauses, no hot-path atomics, use-after-free becomes a clean miss). Ch03 gets one forward sentence.\n- **Budget precedent check (small):** verify ch06's named-budgets section names engine precedents (UE scalability/pool CVars vs. Unity's largely implicit budgets vs. Godot minimal) [verify]; audit expects Tier-2 formalization framing to suffice, so this is a check, not necessarily an expansion.\n\nPolicy: tiered comparison rule in `.claude/skills/book/SKILL.md`.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a3","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-c65b57","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["book","revision","chapter-06"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:50:07.327035Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a89cf8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Repair audit nitpicks: ch01 RQ7 orphaned concept + minor ch05 awareness items","description":"Internal-consistency nits found during the sw-438537 audit and the sw-a93fd7 ch05 pass; none is a comparison fork.\n\n- **ch01 review question 7** asks about \"GPU memory as a cache,\" a concept the ch01 body never introduces (it is ch04 material). Either rewrite the question against ch01 content or add a forward-pointing sentence in the body.\n- **ch03 learn-bullet** promising the task-graph-evolution argument is NOT this issue's scope — it is folded into sw-2f2873 (CH03-F1).\n- Optional ch05 awareness items (previously accepted as-is; take only if convenient): the input-frame-timing figure's phase strip omits CLEAR while the prose lists it; the cursor-capture prose says \"locked to the window center,\" a simplification of winit's Locked mode.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a4","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-a89cf8","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["book","bug","nitpick"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:50:16.942738Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e78dea","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add dedicated extension/plugin architecture chapter to the book outline","description":"Author decision 2026-08-19 (recorded in `book/reviews/2026-08-19-ch01-04-comparison-audit.md`): the plugin/extension architecture fork gets a **dedicated chapter** rather than living inside ch02 or ch23.\n\nScope when executed:\n- Create the chapter stub and slot it into `_quarto-book.yml`; numbering intersects the in-flight ch22-26 restructure, so position is an outline call to make at execution time.\n- The chapter owns the Tier-1 comparison: UE C++ module plugins with broad engine-API reach, Unity packages/C# assemblies, Godot GDExtension/addons [verify all], versus Smallworld's narrow per-role registration seams (component types/systems, asset importers, render passes/materials, tool panels — each receiving only the contract for its role, per ch02).\n- Extra weight: voxels ship as the first-class Voxel Plugin, so this chapter carries the proof that the seams are sufficient for a flagship feature.\n- Ch02 keeps its preview and gains a forward pointer (optional rider noted in sw-e1cbe3).\n\nFiled as BACKLOG capture of the decision; scheduling is the author's call.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a7","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-e78dea","target_id":"sw-438537","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["book","outline","feature"]},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:50:23.183913Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-438537","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dfcff810-a995-49d0-822f-9e2dd36920db","text":"## Deliverable extended per author direction\n\nAuthor decided the two outline questions: plugin architecture → **dedicated chapter**; code-first game description → **ch09** (leaning on Godot dropping VisualScript in 4.0 and UE6 dropping Blueprints as trajectory evidence).\n\nAdded to this issue's worktree alongside the audit report:\n- **Obligation notes planted in stubs** (following ch12's \"Deferred from Chapter 3\" convention): ch08 (ECS object-model comparison; hybrid ECS-vs-side-structures fork with sw-cf6350 benchmark evidence), ch09 (code-first fork home + UE6/Godot trajectory), ch12 (extraction-mechanism fork deferred from ch03; voxel+mesh unified-domain thesis from ch01), ch15 (raster-first/RT-secondary lighting comparison).\n- Audit report's outline-decisions section updated to DECIDED.\n\n**Follow-up issues filed:**\n- sw-2f2873 — Ch03 retrofit (CH03-F1 threading fork, the moderate one, + CH03-F3), PLANNED, depends_on this\n- sw-098dc0 — Ch04 retrofit (F1/F2/F3/F5, optional F4), PLANNED, depends_on this\n- sw-e1cbe3 — Ch01+Ch02 retrofit (CH01-F1, CH02-F1, CH02-F2), PLANNED, depends_on this\n- sw-c65b57 — Ch06 rider (CH03-F2 handle-lifetime GC comparison + budget precedent check), PLANNED, depends_on this\n- sw-a89cf8 — nitpick repairs (ch01 RQ7 + optional ch05 awareness items), PLANNED\n- sw-e78dea — dedicated plugin-architecture chapter (outline addition), BACKLOG capture of the decision\n\nWorktree now holds: the audit report + 4 stub files with obligation notes. Awaiting tophat to walkthrough + merge."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T13:50:35.428516Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
