{"id":"sw-2f2873","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-34364f96-4657-4b58-8c36-43aa37976478","text":"## Done (on issue branch, merge pending batch tophat)\n\n- **CH03-F1:** Added the three-strategy comparison (UE named threads + Task Graph; Unity main-thread orchestration + job declarations + verified `RenderingThreadingMode` graphics-jobs modes; ND fibers with the tooling cost) and the per-alternative winner rationale (latency isolation by construction; thread-as-owner matches CSP and Rust; native debugger/profiler visibility). The learn-bullet promise is delivered **in timeless form per the author's no-roadmap-in-book correction**: the split pools and the task graph are presented as points on one ownership architecture (scoped fork-join islands generalizing into a dependency-scheduled graph as cross-system interdependence grows), with the staging left to `capability-tiers.md`, which already has the Threading tier row (pools → mature split → task-graph). Learn-bullet rewritten accordingly.\n- **CH03-F3:** Unity line added to the Extraction Contract (verified: Entities Graphics batching into `BatchRendererGroup` draw commands); \"both engines\" → \"all of these engines.\"\n- Editorial: one pre-existing spaced-hyphen clause link fixed.\n\nRenders clean; 8,595 words (in range). ~620 words added. All engine claims vendor-doc verified this session."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T14:05:57.910919Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
