{"id":"sw-098dc0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b7ed371f-4342-4821-91fb-1b79c6b5d332","text":"## Done (on issue branch, merge pending batch tophat)\n\n- **F1:** Unity added to the pipeline comparison (\"overlap by configuration rather than architecture\": render-thread translation + graphics-jobs fan-out; verified `RenderingThreadingMode` docs).\n- **F2:** Extrapolation callout now names the one engine that ships it (Unity `Rigidbody.interpolation` `Extrapolate`, verified, including its documented overshoot/snap-back artifact) and adds why Smallworld's policy is engine-wide rather than per-body. Per author correction: states plainly that only Unity ships it.\n- **F5:** Per author correction, the \"separation is universal\" sentence was rewritten rather than contradicted: universal availability is not universal default; Unreal's stock tick is variable-delta with substepping as bounded semi-fixed (verified UE docs) and the fixed async physics tick as opt-in.\n- **F3:** Per the no-roadmap rule, the book now commits to the **recovery walk as Smallworld's designed end-point** (invariant makes it additive; fatal-with-grace is the fallback of last resort, not the design target). Staging remains in `capability-tiers.md` (already marked: fatal-with-grace tier → recovery-walk tier).\n- **F4 (taken):** feedback-channel precedent note added — Unity `FrameTimingManager` (verified: multi-frame delivery delay, DRS/adaptive-perf as consumers, mirroring our readback-ring semantics) and UE stat/CSV telemetry, versus Smallworld's typed in-loop channel.\n- Roadmap sweep: `// v1:`/`// v2:` comments removed from `LatencyMode`; \"future refinement\" → \"opt-in tool\". Editorial: two spaced-hyphen links and one grammar typo (\"which will discuss next\") fixed.\n\nRenders clean, zero dash violations, 12,038 words. All engine claims vendor-doc verified this session."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T14:16:12.7463Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
