{"id":"sw-e1cbe3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-62f69ef2-5000-4ab9-9566-cf27ed4af4ba","text":"## Done (on issue branch, merge pending batch tophat)\n\n- **CH01-F1:** wgpu section now completes the survey: Unity's per-target device abstraction and Godot 4's `RenderingDevice` over Vulkan/D3D12/Metal (verified against Godot docs) join the existing UE RHI treatment, sharpening the argument to \"every cross-platform engine owns this layer; the question is who maintains it.\"\n- **CH02-F1:** Unity assembly definitions added to the boundary-enforcement comparison, plus the per-alternative rationale the prose lacked: all three mechanisms make violations loud; the crate variant adds a compile-checked permitted surface (API-crate re-exports) and no runtime reflection bypass, which C# assemblies cannot claim.\n- **CH02-F2:** Unity's opaque subsystem init added to the boot survey with the honest trade-off framing.\n- Optional riders (ch01 catalog connective, ch02 pointers to the plugin chapter / ch09) skipped: the plugin chapter is BACKLOG (sw-e78dea) and pointers to unwritten homes would dangle.\n\nBoth chapters render clean. ~230 words added total."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T14:18:24.08418Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
