{"id":"sw-c65b57","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6962a535-60fa-4257-a012-2aeb750165be","text":"## Done (on issue branch, merge pending batch tophat)\n\n- **CH03-F2 (landed in ch06 §Identity Before Address):** \"Identity is where the engines converge; lifetime is where they fork\" — UE UObject mark-and-sweep GC + `TWeakObjectPtr` (with tuning cost), Unity's split managed-GC/explicit-destroy model, Godot `RefCounted` + manual `RID`s, versus Smallworld's single-owner + generational handles where refcounts answer residency (evictable-at-zero, never evicted-at-zero) and reclamation is a budget decision. Per-alternative rationale: no collection passes or graph-proportional cost vs. GC; no hot-path count traffic and no cycle-pinned GPU memory vs. refcounting; the honest cost (no automatic lifetime extension) is framed as the residency invariant's defined-miss feature. Consistent with the chapter's existing evictability rule. No ch03 edit needed — its existing vs-refcounting argument plus this deep treatment covers the fork.\n- **Budget precedent check:** the section already had the platform-cert grounding and architectural-vs-retrofitted framing; added one engine sentence (UE's explicit texture streaming pool limit vs. Unity's implicit budgets).\n\nRenders clean, no dash violations. ~310 words added."},"created_at":"2026-08-19T14:28:00.021198Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.235 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
